the Risk Gaps card listed \\\\\\\"Programming Languages\\\\\\\" by name, and a \\\\\\\"Competency Gap Alert\\\\\\\" box appeared stating \\\\\\\"1 competency below recommended level: Programming Languages. Consider increasing training focus or adjusting expectations.\\\\\\\" Then raised Programming Languages back to level 4 (Advanced) via set-level-4: Risk Gaps count returned to 0, Coverage/Avg Level returned to baseline 68%/3.3, and the Competency Gap Alert box disappeared entirely — confirming the risk-gap warning correctly appears when lowering an enabled high-weight competency below its recommended level, names it, and clears once resolved.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"When Programming Languages was lowered below its recommended level, an alert box titled \\\\\\\"Competency Gap Alert\\\\\\\" appeared directly beneath the summary metrics row (Coverage/Avg Level/Critical Path/Risk Gaps cards), i.e. prominently positioned near the summary metrics. It explicitly named the affected competency (\\\\\\\"Programming Languages\\\\\\\") and suggested a concrete corrective action (\\\\\\\"Consider increasing training focus or adjusting expectations.\\\\\\\"), satisfying all three requirements: prominent placement near summary metrics, naming affected competencies, and suggesting corrective action.\"}]}"
